fix(sexbjcam): probe HLS availability instead of guessing from the index

Two defects found by measuring the real responses rather than trusting the
reference notes.

1. The "sort by descending hlsN" rule was backwards.
   The reference card claimed hls2 returns 403 and only a higher number works.
   Measured across 4 independent samples, each on a different video:
     hls2 (.m3u8) -> HTTP 200   (usable)
     hls3 (.txt)  -> HTTP 404   (dead)
   So the old rule reliably picked the dead entry. getStream now probes each
   candidate and keeps only the ones that respond 2xx/3xx. Candidates are
   few (2-3), so the extra request buys certainty instead of a guess.
   Verified 3 runs: each returns "HLS 2" and that URL answers HTTP 200.

2. The embed host was hardcoded as recordplay.biz.
   The site has since moved to playrecord.biz, so the lookup silently found
   no embed iframe and getStream failed with "detail page has no recordplay
   embed entry". Both meta.ts and stream.ts matched on that domain literal.
   Replaced with isEmbedUrl(), which recognises the /e/{hash} and
   /embed/{hash} path shapes, so a future host change does not break it.

Stream count for this provider drops from 2 to 1 because the dead entry is no
longer reported. Test: sexbjcam 40 posts / meta / 1 stream -> PASSED.
